

Structure of a PDF:
	- is just a collection of instructions placing text strings at geometric coordinates.
		ex: Put the word 'Benefits' at coordinate X:50, Y:100 using Arial 24pt Bold."
	- Font can at letter granularity, as each letter can have its own font.
	- what can be used in order to find if it a 
		- line
		- paragraph
		- header
		- Footer
		- Title
		- Sub title
	- bbox, bounding box, for
		- images
		- text region
		- e.t.c

